       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, and that is about five times the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, or 3,000 mg/day in some references. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nIt may be a typo. Some possibilities:\n- **425 mg TID**, which is unusual because metformin doesn't come in that strength.\n- **850 mg TID**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the standard maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg TID**, or another regimen.\n\nIf you really do want 4250 mg per dose, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
